novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-002.md:5:"Take it, Garr," Elys said, the line as private as a coin counted in the dark, and he closed his hand around the ivory as if she had lent him a piece of herself.
novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-001.md:11:"Take it," she says, and the sound of her voice is less than a vow but more than a promise. "Take it, Garr."
novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-001.md:15:Marta's answer is a whisper that the leaves nearly steal. "I'll watch. I won't tell."
novel/chapters/ch-01/scenes/s-001.md:25:"I will wait," she says, as plain and as absolute. The bench between them keeps their knees from touching, and still their bodies make a map of decisions—small, stubborn.
